    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293-a2">

                <pb facs="0536" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg408"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    223—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Dr. Busch to Mr.
                            Kasson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1885-02-03"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 3,
                    1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned has the honor, replying to the esteemed note of the 29th ultimo,
                    to inform Mr. John A. Kasson, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary
                    of the United States of America, that measures have been instituted to cause a
                    close investigation of the case of Ernst F. Heitmüller, of Hüpede, to be made by
                    the appropriate authority.</p>
                <p>While the undersigned reserves to himself to make a further communication, he
                    avails, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>BUSCH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
